case: e_limit_after_see
ac: AC-33 (e), reading per SPEC 5.0: also for `last n`
kind: query (rows sent to the client and rendered in the view)
compile: ostrel check exits 0 with no diagnostic; the `see` rule is inside the pushdown subset
  (ARCHITECTURE 9: field access, `or`, comparison with `me`)
principals: alice, bob (development identities, debug build, AC-12)
given: alice has made ten Note rows, each accepted before the next:
  pos  body  shared
  1    p1    false
  2    p2    false
  3    s3    true
  4    p4    false
  5    s5    true
  6    s6    true
  7    p7    false
  8    s8    true
  9    p9    false
  10   p10   false
probes:
  1. bob opens the view (the must deny case)
     first column, `sort pos limit 3`: s3, s5, s6 in this order
     last column, `sort pos last 3`: s5, s6, s8 in this order
     no row with shared = false reaches bob's client, neither in a Snapshot nor in the view
  2. alice opens the view (control)
     first column: p1, p2, s3
     last column: s8, p9, p10
final db: unchanged by both probes
must not, for bob: first column s3 alone (limit applied before the rule), last column s8 alone
  (last applied before the rule), fewer than three rows, or any p row
